[0.001, "o", "it\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m.                                                                                                                                                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 11 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 12 \u001b[22m ### New Concepts Required\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 13 \u001b[22m - **Group**: the container and consistency boundary for shared expenses — owns its members, its expenses, and therefore all balances and settlement s\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  \u001b[11G\u001b[22muggestions. Balances never cross group boundaries.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m...\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m47\u001b[13G\u001b[22mResource-oriented REST surface\u001b[44Gnested under groups\u001b[64G(group\u001b[71G, m\u001b[75Gmbers, expenses, balances, set\u001b[106Glements).\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m48\u001b[11G\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 49 \u001b[22m ### Key Design Decisions\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m56\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Tech\u001b[20Gstack**: Node.js 24 +\u001b["]
[0.009, "o", "42GTypeScript (modern, available locally, strong test tooling) vs.\u001b[106GGo (available\u001b[121Gstrong typ\u001b[134G, but \u001b[141Gore boilerplate\u001b[157Gfor\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m a small API) vs. Python 3.9 (outdated system interpreter). → **Recommend TypeScript on Node.js** with a lightweight HTTP framework and a mainstream \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtest runner; to be confirmed.                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m50\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m-\u001b[13G**Tech\u001b[20Gstack**:\u001b[29GNode.js\u001b[37G24\u001b[40G+\u001b[42GTypeScript\u001b[53G(modern,\u001b[62Gavailable\u001b[72Glocally,\u001b[81Gstrong\u001b[88Gtest\u001b[93Gtooling)\u001b[102Gvs.\u001b[106GGo\u001b[109G(available,\u001b[121Gstrong\u001b[128Gtyping,\u001b[136Gbut\u001b[140Gmore\u001b[145Gboilerplate\u001b[157Gfor\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m a small API) vs. Python 3.9 (outdated system interpreter). → \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mLocally available toolchains are Node.js 24, "]
[0.001, "o", "Go, and Python 3.9 (no Java/.NET). \u001b[48;2;2;40;0m**Recom\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mmend TypeScript on Node.js** with a lightweight HTTP framework and a mainstream test runner; to be confirmed.                                        \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m51\u001b[11G\u001b[22m- **Money\u001b[21Gre\u001b[24Gresentation**: integer minor units (simple, fast, exact; requires conversion at API boundary) vs. arbitrary-precision decimal library (n\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m atural input format, extra dependency) vs. floats (rejected — violates requirement). → **Recommend integer minor units internally** (with BigInt or s\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m afe-integer bounds check), with a clearly defined API wire format (see next decision).\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 52 \u001b[22m - **API wire format for amounts**: decimal string (e.g., \"12.34\" — human-friendly, avoids JSON float parsing) vs. integer cents (unambiguous, less fr\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m iendly) vs. JSON number (risk of float coercion"]
[0.001, "o", "). → **Recommend decimal string on input and output**, parsed strictly into minor units; reject anythi\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m ng with excess precision.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 53 \u001b[22m - **Remainder allocation in equal splits**: give extra cents to first participants in request order vs. a stable sort order (e.g., member id) vs. to \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m the payer. → **Recommend deterministic order by participant order as submitted (or member id)**, documented and tested; exact choice fixed in REASONS\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m  Canvas.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allow\u001b[12Gd by auto mode\u001b[27Gclassif\u001b[35Ger\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[13C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1m 22s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m7.7k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l"]
